From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:40:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: wait for the prerast producer before viewport runs biblioklept

A gpu_prerast draw that selects a viewport per primitive runs three
compute kernels on the compute queue: the lowered VS, the GS kernel
(when there is a GS), then the viewport run builder. The run builder
reads the producer's records and its index count, and writes the run
list header that the vertex/tiler queue walks.

The producer kernels end with a CSF sync barrier. That barrier only
signals the compute syncobj for the vertex/tiler queue. It does not stop
the next RUN_COMPUTE on the compute queue, which goes to another
iterator scoreboard. So the run builder could start while the GS kernel
was still writing, read a zero count, and write run_count = 0. The
draw then emitted nothing.

On an Immortalis-G925 (v13), gs_viewport_depth failed in 5 to 7 of 10
runs with nothing drawn in any case:

  FAIL case A_clamp depthL=[1.000000..1.000000] expL=0.250000
       badDepth=1024 badColor=1024

The chunk loop and the tessellation path already wait on all iterator
scoreboards before panlib_vp_runs_launch_struct(). Do the same in
gpu_prerast_draw_generated().

The race is in shared CSF code, so v10-v12 get the same wait. There,
gs_viewport_depth passed because the smaller GPU finished the producer
first. The cost is one compute-queue wait per viewport-run draw.

G925: gs_viewport_depth 10/10, PanProbe Run all 36/36.

---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -4559,8 +4559,16 @@
           * A launch here is recorded after that loop, past TESS_FREE.
           */
          if (!vp_launch) {
+            struct panvk_device *dev = to_panvk_device(cmdbuf->vk.base.device);
             struct panvk_precomp_ctx ctx = panvk_per_arch(precomp_cs)(cmdbuf);

+            /* The run builder reads the VS/GS kernel's records and counts.
+             * Its sync barrier only orders the VT queue, not this compute
+             * queue: without the wait it can run beside the producer and
+             * see a zero count, so the draw emits nothing.
+             */
+            cs_wait_slots(panvk_get_cs_builder(cmdbuf, PANVK_SUBQUEUE_COMPUTE),
+                          dev->csf.sb.all_iters_mask);
             panlib_vp_runs_launch_struct(&ctx, panlib_1d(1),
                                          PANLIB_BARRIER_CSF_SYNC, *use);
             gpu_prerast_wait_compute(cmdbuf);
--
